.TH CHTTPSVR_REQ_QUERY_OOM 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_req_query_oom \- check whether chttpsvr_req_query ran out of memory
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

bool chttpsvr_req_query_oom(const chttpsvr_req *req);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns true when an allocation for the query string of this request
failed because the library ran out of memory.  Two allocations can
fail this way.  The first is the growth of the result array inside
chttpsvr_req_query.  The second is the one-time, shared parse of the
query string, which chttpsvr_req_query and chttpsvr_req_query_one each
start lazily on their first use.

chttpsvr_req_query gives NULL and a count of 0 in two cases: the
requested key is absent, or a lack of memory stopped the build of the
result array.  Use this function to tell the two cases apart after any
NULL return from chttpsvr_req_query.

The flag latches.  After the library sets it, it stays true for the
rest of the request, whatever query calls follow.  This function
returns false when req is NULL.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
true; an allocation for the query string of this request failed out of
memory.
false; no allocation error happened, or req is NULL.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_req_query (3),
.BR chttpsvr_req_query_one (3)
